**Issue**: #372
**Date**: 2026-09-07
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG
**Related Spec**: specs/369-detect-execute-remediation-loops-and-close-workers-on-cancel/

Feature: Bounded operator recovery of an exhausted delivery
  Ordinary resume previously offered no explicit path out of a remediation loop.
  A single-use checkpoint authorization permits one repair without weakening gates.

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Explicit exact-checkpoint authorization
    Given a legacy delivery stopped after 13 implementation attempts
    And the operator supplies its current recovery identity and a reason
    When execute consumes the authorized retry
    Then exactly one repair worker may run
    And the issue queue, prior attempts, work and completed stages are preserved

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: No implicit allowance or authorization replay
    Given a stopped checkpoint with a consumed or stale recovery identity
    When ordinary resume, stale-lease recovery, an upgrade or concurrent replay is attempted
    Then no new repair allowance is granted
    And no more than one consumer can dispatch the originally authorized attempt

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Failed recovery stays bounded
    Given an authorized recovery worker has been dispatched
    When it fails without advancement or dispatch becomes ambiguous
    Then no automatic follow-on remediation starts
    And reentry cannot replay the consumed attempt
    And the failed evidence remains available

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Passed work completes normal delivery
    Given an authorized recovery produces a validated passed handoff
    When execute advances the stage
    Then every remaining review, verification and exact-head delivery gate remains required
    And the next stage retains its normal bounded remediation policy

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Intervention and ownership remain fail-closed
    Given retry encounters intervention, blocked evidence or uncertain ownership
    When the operator supplies a recovery identity
    Then execute refuses to bypass the blocker or launch duplicate work
    And only positively absent recorded panes can be reconciled
    And unrelated and reused pane identities remain protected

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: Discoverable and verified operator recovery
    Given an eligible exhausted checkpoint is inspected through the installed command surface
    When the operator reads status or the stopped command result
    Then output names the reason and current recovery identity with an exact retry command
    And stale-lease recovery is distinguished from retry authorization
    And actual isolated command and fresh registered smoke delivery evidence prove the contract
